<header><small>Technical investigation · 11 October 2026 · Proposal awaiting user decision</small><h1>Render existing components in Visual</h1><p class="lede">The components already render. The editor needs to discover their real entrypoints and call them with authored sample values.</p><p class="note">Recommendation: build a preview-first iteration for ordinary component factories. Do not require component authors to add <code>uiDefinition</code>, editor registration, or a custom visual adapter.</p></header>
<nav aria-label="Contents"><a href="#evidence">What was verified</a><a href="#gaps">What is missing</a><a href="#proposal">Proposed implementation</a><a href="#scope">Scope and decisions</a><a href="#validation">Validation</a></nav>
<section id="evidence"><h2>What was verified</h2><p>The TypeScript checker recovered the public parameter fields and return shapes of six named exports. A DOM probe mounted Button, ScrollArea and TextEditor directly. A separate browser probe mounted ScrollArea and TextEditor from their existing served exports with authored sample content. Component source was unchanged.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Current shape</th><th>First-iteration implications</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Button</td><td>Optional scalar properties; optional activation callback. Returns a DOM element.</td><td>Strong first case: edit label/text/disabled values; omit optional callback.</td></tr>
<tr><td>TextEditor</td><td>Required mode; text and optional diff lines; optional callbacks. Returns an object containing an element and input.</td><td>Strong first case: text, read-only state and modes. Derive enum and structured sample types from source.</td></tr>
<tr><td>ScrollArea</td><td>Required label; axis; optional DOM content. Returns an element.</td><td>Scalar properties are straightforward. Meaningful content needs an authored sample setup that constructs DOM content; it is not a JSON value.</td></tr>
<tr><td>TabPanel / ViewPanel</td><td>Require selection callbacks as well as data. ViewPanel and ViewToolbar share a source file today.</td><td>No intrinsic service dependency, but they need callable sample inputs. Defer initially; separate the two components before treating that file as one component.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tree</td><td>Generic data, sets, selectors, rendering and expansion callbacks.</td><td>Sample data alone is insufficient. Defer until callable inputs and generic sample types are supported.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p><strong>Limits:</strong> these probes used selected, known exports. They do not establish automatic component discovery, generic invocation, isolation, or arbitrary component compatibility. No complete repository inventory is claimed.</p>
